  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Inclusive Emergency Response for Older Men, Women and Older People with Disabilities affected by Cyclone Idai in Sofala and Tete Provinces &#x2013; Mozambique.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increased protection and inclusion of older women, men and people with disabilities in the project target locations</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will build on existing interventions, largely financed by the DEC. The project therefore proposes to continue providing basic essential services for OP and their families, both direct intervention and through Outreach Teams, that will ensure that they are protected, safe and secure. This shall be done through case management and referrals, psychosocial support (PSS), NFI (Seed) distributions, and health (basic health care and home-based support).</narrative>
  </description>
